{{also|Rùssia|Rússia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁reh₁- (row)}}
1530s, from {{bor|en|ML.|Russi||the people of Russia}}, from {{der|en|orv|Русь||[[Rus]]}} (whence {{cog|ar|رُوس}} and {{cog|gkm|Ῥῶς}}), which originally referred to a group of [[Varangian]]s who established themselves near [[Kiev]] in the 9th century and ruled [[Kievan Rus]]; probably from {{der|en|urj-fin-pro|*roocci}}, from {{der|en|non-oen|*roþs-||related to rowing}}; related to {{der|en|non|Roþrslandi||the land of rowing}}, an older name of [[Roslagen]], where the [[Finn]]s first encountered the [[Swede]]s. Ultimately from {{der|en|non|róðr||steering oar}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*rōþrą||rudder}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁reh₁-||to row}}.

===Pronunciation===
