* {{rhymes|en|ʌʃə|s=2}}
* {{homophones|en|rusher}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|~|s}}

# {{sid|en|Q159}}{{place|en|A [[transcontinental]] <<country>> in <<r/Eastern Europe,North Asia>>|caplc=Moscow|official=Russian Federation}}. It borders the [[Pacific Ocean|Pacific]] and [[Arctic Ocean|Arctic]] Oceans and the [[Baltic Sea|Baltic]], [[Black Sea|Black]], and [[Caspian Sea|Caspian]] Seas. Part of the [[Soviet Union]] from 1917 through 1991.
# {{lb|en|historical|loosely}} The [[Union of Soviet Socialist Republics]] (a very common name, although more formally Russia, the [[RSFSR]], was one of several constituent republics of the USSR).
# {{lb|en|historical}} The [[Russian Empire]]; the [[tsarist]] [[empire]] in Russia lasting from 1721 to 1917.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1911|title=Ukraine|work=1911 Encyclopædia Britannica|passage=Ukraine (“frontier”), the name formerly given to a district of European '''Russia''', now comprising the governments of Kharkov, Kiev, Podolia and Poltava.|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/1911_Encyclop%C3%A6dia_Britannica/Ukraine}}
# {{lb|en|historical|dated}} [[Kievan Rus]]; the [[medieval]] [[East Slavic]] state centered in [[Kiev]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1911|title=Ukraine|work=1911 Encyclopædia Britannica|passage=Ukraine (“frontier”), the name formerly given to a district of European '''Russia''', now comprising the governments of Kharkov, Kiev, Podolia and Poltava.|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/1911_Encyclop%C3%A6dia_Britannica/Ukraine}}
# {{lb|en|dated|countable}} Any of several East Slavic states [[descend|descended]] from Kievan Rus, typically including Russia ([[Great Russia]]), [[Belarus]] ([[White Russia]]) and [[Ukraine]] ([[Little Russia]]).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1842|author=George Eliot|section=Letter to Cara Bray|title=Selections from George Eliot's letters|page=24|passage=Or rather if I be attaining a better autocratship than that of the Emperor of all the '''Russias''' — the empire over self.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914|title=Russia and the Russian People|passage=Then there is White Russia and Red Russia, Great Russia and Little Russia, Russia of the Frozen North and Russia of the Far East — a '''Russia''' equally dangerous to every one of her neighbours {{...}}}}

